{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788976432,"nonce":"MHLBXAVArhFZjgkxbVuXZp6dmkc=","title":"An unresolvable native panics the promoter thread instead of trapping at the call","message":"`llvm/function/mod.rs:268` resolves a native and panics when it cannot:\n\n    .resolve_function(\"std\", name)\n    .unwrap_or_else(|_| panic!(\"Failed to resolve native function: {}\", name))\n\nThat runs on `beadie-promoter-N`, so a missing symbol takes down a background\ncompile thread rather than the call site that needs it. The same file already\nhas the right behaviour for this case elsewhere -- `natives.rs` logs\n\"native ... unresolved (...); generating call-time trap\" and emits a stub, so\nthe program only fails if it actually calls the thing.\n\nReproduced with `--mode jit` on `examples/heaps_base2d/bin/game.hl`: repeated\n\n    Failed to resolve native function: hlp_alloc_obj_sized\n    thread 'beadie-promoter-1' panicked at crates/ash/src/llvm/function/mod.rs:268:33\n\n`hlp_alloc_obj_sized` is a recent addition to `std/src/obj.rs`. The runtime that\nsample loads is its own staged `libhl.1.dylib`, which predates the symbol, so\nevery promotion of a body containing a `New` kills the promoter.\n\nTwo things to fix:\n\n  1. Route this through the same call-time trap path as every other unresolved\n     native. A background compile thread must not panic over a symbol the\n     program may never reach.\n  2. The release `libash_std.dylib` can lag the release `ash` that emits calls\n     into it. `build.rs` falls back to the debug cdylib in a release build,\n     which masks the mismatch during local work and lets it surface only where\n     a separate runtime is staged. The fallback should at least be loud.","files":null}]}